Function Area2(Y : Numeric[I] ; X : ascending numeric[I]; I : IndexTy~~
pe)
Title: Area2 (Y,X,I)
Description: Computes the area under a curve given by the points in (~~
X,Y), using the trapezoidal rule.  Like the built-in Area function, e~~
xcept the bulit-in one has a problem with local indexes, and also thi~~
s one allows X to be separate from I.  This does only indefinite inte~~
gration -- it doesn't have the bounds of a definite integral that the~~
 built-in Area function has.~
(Note: the built-in function can be used for both these purposes in A~~
nalytica 4.0 or later)
Definition: var pos := cumulate(1,I);~
var prevY := Slice(Y,I,if pos>1 then pos-1 else 1);~
var prevX := Slice(X,I,if pos>1 then pos-1 else 1);~
sum( (X-prevX) * (Y+prevY)/2, I )
